{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Go, my people, enter your chambers.</b> According to Rabbi Moses the Cohen's view, they would shut themselves in Jerusalem because of Sennacherib." "<b>Hide yourself.</b> Some say that it comes by way of holders of final he, for it is found with feminine language, like וחטאת עמך (and the sin of your people) (Exodus 5:16), and Rabbi Judah the Grammarian, of blessed memory, said that חבי is a noun on the pattern of שבי (Isaiah 20:4). The first is the truth."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "Resolved the abbreviation נ\"ע as 'of blessed memory' (נוח נפשו / נטריא רחמתא), standard for Ibn Ezra's eulogistic formula after a deceased scholar."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:19.626009578Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}